# Kkairojan Minotaur

## Lore

The Kkairojan are one of three Minotaur tribes that buried themselves under what is now the Sandy Desert some seventy thousand years ago, meaning to atone for their ancestors'' service to the Old Ones. Their repentance lasted a few thousand years. Tired of bearing blame for deeds they had not done, they reasoned that if the world would shun them anyway, it might as well have cause, and they went back to the worship their forefathers had sworn off. Today the whole tribe serves the Old Ones willingly and looks for a way to wake them.

They survived underground by eating a fourth tribe that had gone below with them, by raiding the surface at night, and by keeping slaves as livestock. When an Earthshaker broke their caverns open they read it as their sleeping masters reaching out to free them, and counted it a blessing that not one of them died in the collapse. Within three days all thirteen hundred had vanished into the desert, after a long battle with the Adraodan tribe that ended only when the Kkairojan drove their cousins off with magic.

Their aim is to slip into the civilized lands, found new cults of the Old Ones, gather worshippers and follow the leads they already hold toward awakening their gods.

**Alignment:** Evil. Nearly all are diabolic or miscreant, with a handful aberrant or anarchist.

**Physical Appearance:** Horned and bull-headed like any Minotaur and powerfully built, but of a lighter frame than their surface kin, the mark of ages spent below ground. They are pale, anywhere from whitish to light grey, with dark hair and yellow-green eyes.

**Height:** About 8 to 9.6 feet (2.4 to 2.8 m). **Weight:** 400 to 700 pounds (180 to 315 kg).

**Average Life Span:** 400 years; few pass 500. **Average Level of Experience:** 1st to 4th.

**Habitat:** Headed for the Baalgor Wastelands, the Old Kingdom, the Western Empire, the Yin-Sloth Jungles and the Land of the South Winds.

**Enemies:** Everything good, and the Adraodan Minotaurs above all. **Allies:** The forces of evil, demons included.

**Favorite Weapons:** None yet.

## GM Notes

This is a villain''s race. Every Kkairojan is a cannibal and a willing servant of the Old Ones, and the book treats the tribe as a spreading threat: once clear of the Wastelands it will break into scores of bands of 13 to 30, with the odd pair or lone agent, and carry its cults across the world.

The tribe is led by Gruegas Wierdling, a diabolic 8th level witch and Disciple of the Old Ones, backed by five 4th level witches sworn to the same masters.

An alchemist may pay up to 1500 gold for a Minotaur horn, though buyers are wary because a bull''s horn looks much the same.
